Z||000022||Jncomutt||12-04-2001||11:13 AM||||I know this is a bit off subject, but for the first time ever, someone is going to agree with BlackStang.  That person is me.  Jaei sun is the defender of all rice.  In my opinion (NOTE: this is not fact, one persons opinion vs another.. hehe), Jaei sun is set out to own the very 1st rice fiero.  I'm feeling the white accents, the big silly vinal sunshade, prob. clear tails, clear bumper/marker lights...  Sorry Jaei sun.  I think your car looks great.  I think riced hondas look good sometimes too.  I would respect the work and effort (you have an AWESOME paint job) if the car was foreign, but, its domestic.  ||||reg||1
Z||000023||Jaei Sun||12-04-2001||01:17 PM||||Not starting a flame here<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Jaei sun is set out to own the very 1st rice fiero. I'm feeling the white accents, the big silly vinal sunshade, prob. clear tails, clear bumper/marker lights<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I won't be the first<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/4_3_1.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Indy2-a.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Indy3-a.jpg"> <P>And as for the Sunshade when has that been considered riced?  I know at least 4 people with PONTIAC there... So rather than having letters there I have a solid color that makes it rice?<P>As for Clear tails, MinnGreenGT and Nashco must be ricers now too by that statement:<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/GTfin06.jpg"> ||||reg||1
