Z||000025||SLAMMED87GT||12-04-2001||01:36 PM||||Looks like a bunch of us MN guys are rice!!!!<P>Here's mine. I LIKE the tips on my car, I LIKE the higher wing, and I LIKE that it has 17's and lowered. Does this make my car rice? NO. It makes my car look, handle, and sound JUST THE WAY I LIKE IT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fiero10-01.jpg"> <P>It's My Pontiac Fiero GT and nothing else.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Pfierosig2_1.jpg"> <P><P>------------------<BR>3" Drop, 17" Primax 618s/Nitto540 205/40, 4" Monza exhaust, Mudstain decklid scoop, 7" wing stands, Clear front and rear lights, custom interior, all options...that's all hehe.||||reg||4
Z||000026||kneebarx||12-04-2001||02:35 PM||||I guess you guys are forgetting the meaning behind rice.  It's making non performance cars, look like they're performance cars by dressing them up.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000027||kneebarx||12-04-2001||02:36 PM||||Rice or not, Slams car is phat!||||reg||1
Z||000028||Pyric||12-04-2001||03:53 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by kneebarx:<BR><B>I guess you guys are forgetting the meaning behind rice.  It's making non performance cars, look like they're performance cars by dressing them up.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Exactly, Hondas and other such "Ricer" cars are a dime a dozen.  They're everywhere and no matter how much money is poured into them the owner will NEVER get it back out. <P>At least Fieros have Sports car potential, and have the possibility of their value increasing over time.  No one is willing to pay 3500 for a 1985 Honda.  <P>No offence to anyone... but the fact is even though I own a Nissan myself, and it has a lot of power for what it is equipped with... it is no Fiero... and I don't try to make it one.  If it were a Skyline... that would be a different story.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>But hey, whatever floats your boat.<P>...Almost forgot... the number one difference between a ricer car and a non-ricer car is the fact that a $500 exhaust system on a non-ricer car makes it sound like a muscle car. <P>A $500 exhaust system on a ricer car... Sounds like a Weed-Eater. <P>------------------<BR>"Never offend people with style when you can offend them with substance." <BR>--Sam Brown<p>[This message has been edited by Pyric (edited 12-04-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000029||REDHOTT88||12-04-2001||05:13 PM||||If it's made in Japan IT'S RICE...<P>No offense... but I'm old enough to know when the whole "rice " thing started. (It actually started with Motorcycles, ...)<P>------------------<BR>Steve<BR><B>1988 Formula 2.8L</B> V6 5 speed<BR><FONT COLOR="ffoooo"> (Red & shiny all over - with all the options!)</FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000030||DRH||12-04-2001||05:29 PM||||I like rice... especially the kind you get in a Chinese restraunt, fried with all that other "stuff" mixed in with it. Really good with almond chicken or sweet and sour chicken over it.<P>Beyond that, the word obviously generates more confusion than communication, why use it?<P>And what's wrong with Kid Rock?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>||||reg||10
