Z||000034||PAUL88GT||12-04-2001||06:35 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by REDHOTT88:<BR><B>If it's made in Japan IT'S RICE...<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I doubt very many Honda's are made in Japan these days. <P>It may be better to say: If it is engineered in Japan It's Rice ...<P>||||reg||1
Z||000035||Pyric||12-04-2001||06:58 PM||||Not necessarily engineered either.  And just for your info the car "Ricer" concept was quite different than the motorcycle "Rice rocket" concept.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>PART of the ORIGINAL naming scheme was because the cars were made it Japan AND Korea.  Besides basing it on origin is no longer valid.  They were econoboxes that came from Japan.  NOW they are NOT (most anyway) and the name stuck.<P>Besides, some Japanese cars (Nissan Skyline) produce more HP than most of us will ever see.  So much in fact, they're not even street legal in the US. <P>||||reg||1
Z||000036||sloth85GT||12-04-2001||07:13 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Jaei Sun:<BR><B>Can someone tell me why that Civic is "riced"?  I don't see any stickers or body kit.  Just looks like he/she bought some aftermarket rims for it.<P>So does buying aftermarket rims for a car make it rice?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>No it doesn't, but buying aftermarket rims for a CIVIC does make it rice!!! Waste......<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.mts.net/~kuzma/fieronl.gif">     <BR>Dan<BR>1985 Silver GT||||reg||1
Z||000037||DKOV||12-04-2001||07:26 PM||||OK then... let's get this all ironed out.<P>Hopped up Japanease car = Rice<BR>Hopped up Italian car = Pasta<BR>Hopped up German car = Kraut<BR>Hopped up British car = Mutton<BR>Hopped up American car = Meatball<P>Add all this to the FLAMES in this thread...<P>We've got a good 'ol fashion cook out and we're ALL invited!!!<P>Add up your "collection" and what kind of food are you?  I'm a Mutton Meatball Pasta kinda guy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>DKOV -||||reg||1
Z||000038||Reality||12-04-2001||07:27 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Jaei Sun:<BR><B>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/4_3_1.jpg">  </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Anyone know who's car this is? I got to see it in Dayton, OH at Crusiefest, and it is one sweet car. Actually this car was one of the first Fiero's I had ever really seen and actually knew what the car was. I guess it was kind of what influenced me to get one. Oh well just curious if anyone knew who the owner was. <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/realitysignature_1.gif"> ||||reg||1
