Z||000040||BlackStang95||12-04-2001||09:43 PM||||"I guess you guys are forgetting the meaning behind rice. It's making non performance cars, look like they're performance cars by dressing them up."<P>exactly right.  The fiero has real performance.  So lowering and rims wouldn't be rice on them.  Those pics jaei posted are though....ugh.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000041||Mach10||12-04-2001||09:49 PM||||Yeah... In general, I am NOT a fan of high-profile spoilers in any way shape or form. But that's not to say that it can't be done... I just haven't seen it done well... Ever. <P>Rice isn't rims and a spoiler. It's rims and a spoiler on a car that cannot possibly benefit from it without some serious work. But hey, if it's got the cahones to back 'em up, more power to ya.||||reg||13
Z||000042||Jncomutt||12-04-2001||10:46 PM||||Slammed87GT, I didn't that having certain things makes ones car Rice.  As I mentioned, it depends on the car.  Your car looks great, as I had mentioned Jaei Suns did as well.  I love all fieros, and think yours looks sweet.  Adding, x,x,x,x,x and x to a Honda makes it rice.  But adding the above to a domestic doens't neccessily make it riced.  Honda + addons always = rice.  Domestic + same addons does not neccesaily = rice.  I think your car is awesome, and with the same mods that can be done to jaei sun, his just has a "Rice" look for some reason.||||reg||1
Z||000043||Pyric||12-05-2001||09:59 AM||||Spoilers have no aerodynamic effect until the car is going in excess of 80mph (I think it was 80).<P>Anyway, most of the cars with the aftermarket spoilers will rarely if ever get up to a speed where a significant difference is felt.<P>And then... if the rest of your car lacks the aerodynamic qualities... it defeats the purpose.  <P>On a fiero... sure it works.  On a Civic... No.. it is a waste of money.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>"Never offend people with style when you can offend them with substance." <BR>--Sam Brown||||reg||1
Z||000044||FieroLisa||12-05-2001||01:18 PM||||Hmm my rims have japanese on them (came that way)...does that make it rice? <P>I think rims are a good addition to many cars, within reason....13" wire rims or 18" niches may not work on a Honda or Cavalier, but who cares if the owner throws on some good lookin 15" rims on their car? <P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.webjolt.f2s.com/pictures/fierolisa.gif">       <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa" TARGET=_blank>FieroLisa's Website</A>*<A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/ncfieros/" TARGET=_blank>NC Tarheels Fieros Site</A><P>AIM: FieroLisa||||reg||1
Z||000045||SLAMMED87GT||12-05-2001||01:38 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Jncomutt:<BR><B>Slammed87GT, I didn't that having certain things makes ones car Rice.  As I mentioned, it depends on the car.  Your car looks great, as I had mentioned Jaei Suns did as well.  I love all fieros, and think yours looks sweet.  Adding, x,x,x,x,x and x to a Honda makes it rice.  But adding the above to a domestic doens't neccessily make it riced.  Honda + addons always = rice.  Domestic + same addons does not neccesaily = rice.  I think your car is awesome, and with the same mods that can be done to jaei sun, his just has a "Rice" look for some reason.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I didn't bother me. I just wanted to post another cool Fiero that has come out of MN!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> No, but really, rice the term came a long time ago with the motorcycles, it just seems to have found its way to the cars. <P>It's really almost like a standard car term now! I mean, even the guys that drive them call their cars "rice" or "a riced out car" so to me it's just a basic term people say!<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Pfierosig2_1.jpg"> <P><P>------------------<BR>3" Drop, 17" Primax 618s/Nitto450 205/40, 4" Monza exhaust, Mudstain decklid scoop, 7" wing stands, Clear front and rear lights, custom interior, all options...that's all hehe.||||reg||1
Z||000046||MinnGreenGT||12-05-2001||02:35 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by BlackStang95:<BR><B>...Those pics jaei posted are [rice] though....ugh.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>So my car is suddenly RICE because you don't like my clear taillight treatment?  Whatever...<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/GreenGTbig.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/GTfin07.jpg"> <BR>----------------------------------------<BR>So what the heck is this then...? A Taco?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mustangrig.jpg"> <BR>----------------------------------------<P>Anyway- if you think my clear lenses make my car a ricer, that's your opinion.  I agree with the other real opinions here... If you try to make a lame car into a performance car, that's rice.  If you put stickers all over your car, especially if you don't have the parts to back up the sticker, that's rice.<P>Really though.  I'm not bothered by "rice" or most forms of mods.  I believe that if you like your car well enough to spend <B>your</B> money, to make it unique to your personality.  Great.  Cool. More power to you!  Basically I respect your car, and I expect you to respect mine (I have to deal with this every year at the local "hot rod" show BTW)!<P>------------------<BR>              <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/GreenGT6.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000047||watts||12-05-2001||10:43 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Pyric:<BR><B>some Japanese cars (Nissan Skyline) produce more HP than most of us will ever see.  So much in fact, they're not even street legal in the US. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Just to stir the pot...  Skylines are now certified for import into north america.<P>I've got a few videos of them racing - OMG.<P>Camera mounted on the outside of the car - White lines and trees became a view after a few seconds.<BR>||||reg||1
