Z||000060||Turbo88||12-31-2001||12:23 PM||||Hmm Rice. I sold my ls1 T/A and started the Fiero project specificly to eat ricers. Rice is anything that sounds like a fart or a bumble bee when it drives off. It is any car that has a rear wing so large you no longer have functional use of your rear view mirror. It is having stickers for mods you don't have. It is an exhaust tip as large or larger than your actual muffler. It is owning anything with the "Weapon R" logo on it. It is buying a "cold air induction kit" that pulls air from next to the exhaust manifold. It is making any of the following light up (valve stem covers, door locks, shifter handle, windshield sprayers, ect). It is a carbon fiber hood with a stock engine under it. It is any front facia that looks like a fish.<P>A ricer is anyone that will tell you that the wing on the back adds traction by generating down force (they add traction to the rear tires of a front wheel drive car and next to none of them have any true aerodynamic downforce). It is anyone that believes having a 1.25 inch exhuast pipe flows better with a 6 inch tip than it otherwise would. It is anyone who will argue NOS is nitrous oxide vs a brand of nitrous oxide injection system. And finally, it is anyone who will buy a "Spiral Max turbo air twister"!<P>Of course there are more but this is some of the funniest things I've seen at the local street races!<P>Oh yeah, someone refered to the rice term coming from motorcycles. That term came from HD and HD clone riders refering to full ferring Japanise superbikes. There is one difference though. A CBR929 RR will smoke all but the most extremely modified Harelys out of the box. Where as it takes an extremely modified ricer to beat an ls1 in stock trim. Rice bikes look fast, are fast, and are about the same price as a low to midrange HD. For around 10k you can run 10s out of the box. Rice bikes are not in the same catagory. <p>[This message has been edited by Turbo88 (edited 12-31-2001).]||||reg||1
